---
title: "Create a document template"
sidebar:
  order: 6
---

Design one reusable label, tag, sheet, or document block.

## Steps

{% steps %}

1. Open `Settings` > `Template Editor` and select `Create new template`.
2. Enter a name, description, record type, side count, width, and height.
3. Add text, record-field placeholders, images, lines, or shapes.
4. Use full `Table::Field` placeholders for reusable templates.
5. Preview with long and missing values, then save the template. Saved templates are listed under `Settings` > `Documents` > `Templates`.
6. Open the settings button in the editor to rename the template later. Renaming repoints the print layouts that used the old name.
7. From the `Templates` list, export one template from its row, or all of them from the options menu.
{% /steps %}

{% aside type="tip" %}
Fonts live under `Settings` > `Documents` > `Fonts`. Install a `.ttf` or `.otf` there to use it in a template. An installed font stays on that device, so a template using it asks for a replacement when imported elsewhere.
{% /aside %}

